{{Short description|none}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=May 2018}}
The '''knockout stage of the [[1958 FIFA World Cup]]''' was the second and final stage of the competition, following the group stage. The knockout stage began on 19 June with the quarter-finals and ended on 29 June 1958 with the [[1958 FIFA World Cup final|final match]], held at the [[Råsunda Stadium]] in [[Solna]]. The top two teams from each group (eight in total) advanced to the knockout stage to compete in a [[Single-elimination tournament|single-elimination]] style tournament. A match for third place also was played between the two losing teams of the semi-finals.

[[Brazil national football team|Brazil]] won the final 5–2 against hosts [[Sweden men's national football team|Sweden]] for their first World Cup title.<ref>{{cite news |last=Molinaro |first=John |url=https://www.sportsnet.ca/soccer/world-cup-2014/1958-world-cup-pele-a-star-is-born/ |title=1958 World Cup: Pele—A star is born |website=sportsnet.ca |publisher=[[Sportsnet]] |date=8 June 2014 |access-date=22 May 2018}}</ref>

