==Quarter-finals==

===Brazil vs Wales===
This was the first time both countries faced each other.<ref>{{cite web |title=Wales national football team: record v Brazil |url=https://www.11v11.com/teams/wales/tab/opposingTeams/opposition/Brazil/ |website=www.11v11.com |access-date=30 June 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240524125230/https://www.11v11.com/teams/wales/tab/opposingTeams/opposition/Brazil/ |archive-date=24 May 2024}}</ref> Wales were without [[John Charles]] for the match, as he had been injured in their [[1958 FIFA World Cup Group 3#Play-off: Wales vs Hungary|play-off match]] against [[Hungary national football team|Hungary]].<ref>{{cite web |title=World Cup finals 1958: the last time Wales qualified for a tournament |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2015/oct/11/wales-world-cup-finals-european-championship-brazil-pele |website=The Guardian |access-date=30 June 2026 |date=11 October 2015}}</ref>

Wales were able to hold Brazil to a 0–0 draw for over an hour,<ref>{{cite web |last1=Thomas |first1=Andi |title=From the Jaws of Victory book: Wales at the 1958 World Cup |url=https://thesetpieces.com/latest-posts/jaws-victory-book-wales-1958-world-cup/ |website=The Set Pieces |access-date=30 June 2026 |date=9 June 2022}}</ref> until [[Pelé]] scored in the 66th minute, becoming both the youngest goal scorer in the tournament's history and the first player under the age of 18 to score at a World Cup.<ref>{{cite web |title=World Cup wonder goals: Pele makes history |url=https://www.fifa.com/en/tournaments/mens/worldcup/canadamexicousa2026/articles/pele-goal-brazil-wales-1958 |website=www.fifa.com |access-date=30 June 2026 |date=20 May 2026}}</ref>

