==Semi-finals==

===Brazil vs France===
This was only the second time Brazil and France had ever faced each other, and the first in an official competition,<ref>{{cite web |title=France’s semi-finals at the World Cup |url=https://www.fifa.com/en/articles/world-cup-qatar-2022-france-previous-6-semi-finals-croatia-brazil-germany-portugal-belgium |website=www.fifa.com |access-date=15 May 2026 |date=December 2022}}</ref> having previously faced each other in a [[exhibition match|friendly match]] in [[Rio de Janeiro]] shortly after the [[1930 FIFA World Cup]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Rivals for nearly a century, Brazil and France are evenly matched |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/rivals-nearly-century-brazil-v-113400494.html |website=Yahoo Sports |access-date=15 May 2026 |date=26 March 2026 |archive-date=27 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260327050655/https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/rivals-nearly-century-brazil-v-113400494.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

Early on in the match, French captain [[Robert Jonquet]] tried to make a short pass to [[André Lerond]], but was intercepted by [[Garrincha]]. After passing it to [[Zito (footballer, born 1932)|Zito]], he was able to get the ball to [[Vavá]], who scored Brazil's first goal in the first two minutes.<ref name="Scotsman">{{cite news |title=Brazil show form which made them favourites |work=The Scotsman |issue=35905 |date=25 June 1958 |page=14}}</ref> However, [[Just Fontaine]] was able to score an equalizer for France seven minutes later, which was the first goal Brazil had conceded all tournament.<ref>{{cite news |title=3-GOAL PELE K.O.s FRANCE |work=Daily Express |issue=18066 |date=25 June 1958 |page=14}}</ref> In the 35th minute, Jonquet collided with Brazilian forward [[Vavá]], causing a double fracture in his [[fibula]].<ref name="Jonquet"/> While Jonquet was off the pitch being treated,<ref name="Genius"/> [[Didi (footballer, born 1928)|Didi]] scored in the 39th minute from 22 yards out to make it 2–1, giving Brazil the lead again.<ref name="Scotsman"/> Brazil then scored a third goal just before half-time, but it was disallowed by referee [[Sandy Griffiths|Benjamin Griffiths]] after consulting the linesman.<ref>{{cite news |title=Pele slams three |work=Daily Herald |issue=13160 |date=25 June 1958 |page=10}}</ref>

Despite his injury in the first half, Jonquet returned to the field for the second half as to not leave France with 10 men due to substitutes not being allowed.<ref name="Jonquet">{{cite web |title=Robert JONQUET |url=https://www.fff.fr/equipe-nationale/joueur/8765-jonquet-robert/fiche.html |website=[[Fédération Française de Football]] |access-date=15 May 2026 |archive-date=30 May 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230530140913/https://www.fff.fr/equipe-nationale/joueur/8765-jonquet-robert/fiche.html |url-status=live }}</ref> He was moved to the left side of the field, swapping positions with [[Jean-Jacques Marcel]].<ref name="FRAvBRA">{{cite web |title=FRANCE 2–5 (1–2) BRESIL |url=http://www.fff.fr/cgi-bin/historique/hist_detail.pl?nomatch=245 |website=[[Fédération Française de Football]] |access-date=15 May 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20061208013642/http://www.fff.fr/cgi-bin/historique/hist_detail.pl?nomatch=245 |archive-date=8 December 2006}}</ref> However, he spent most of the match limping on the left wing,<ref name="Genius">{{cite web |title=1958: Boy genius boosts Brazil |url=https://www.uefa.com/european-qualifiers/news/019c-0e6adb9fdf80-0d1cf41ed13a-1000--1958-boy-genius-boosts-brazil/ |website=UEFA.com |access-date=15 May 2026 |language=en |date=29 April 2004 |archive-date=26 November 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221126012605/https://www.uefa.com/european-qualifiers/news/019c-0e6adb9fdf80-0d1cf41ed13a-1000--1958-boy-genius-boosts-brazil/ |url-status=live }}</ref> effectively making it so that France were down to 10 men.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Scheibe |first1=John |title=This day in sports: Brazil's Pelé strikes it big in 1958 World Cup |url=https://www.latimes.com/sports/story/2020-06-24/this-day-in-sports-brazils-pele-strikes-it-big-in-1958-world-cup |website=Los Angeles Times |access-date=16 May 2026 |date=24 June 2020 |archive-date=19 November 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251119002916/https://www.latimes.com/sports/story/2020-06-24/this-day-in-sports-brazils-pele-strikes-it-big-in-1958-world-cup |url-status=live }}</ref>

Following Jonquet's injury, Brazil started dominating the match.<ref name="BDP">{{cite news |title=Brazil's Brilliance |work=Birmingham Daily Post |issue=31146 |page=11 |date=25 June 1958}}</ref> During the second half, [[Pelé]] scored a hat-trick, the first of his international career, in the span of 23 minutes.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Mamrud |first1=Roberto |title=Edson Arantes do Nascimento "Pelé" – Goals in International Matches |url=https://www.rsssf.org/miscellaneous/pele-intlg.html |website=www.rsssf.org |access-date=16 May 2026 |date=23 May 2004 |archive-date=27 June 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190627023832/https://www.rsssf.org/miscellaneous/pele-intlg.html |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Roger Piantoni]] scored a second goal for France in the 83rd minute.<ref name="FRAvBRA"/>

